1
00:00:05,800 --> 00:00:06,840
I'm here to apologize.

2
00:00:08,440 --> 00:00:09,280
Apologize?

3
00:00:09,360 --> 00:00:10,720
You're not running away

4
00:00:11,560 --> 00:00:13,040
just because you fell for my brother, are you?

5
00:00:13,680 --> 00:00:14,440
P'Ing,

6
00:00:14,800 --> 00:00:16,000
we need to sort this out first.

7
00:00:17,840 --> 00:00:19,440
We're in public, you know.

8
00:00:23,920 --> 00:00:24,720
Yok.

9
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:27,440
You said we'd watch the sunrise together, didn't you?

10
00:00:34,480 --> 00:00:35,520
P'Ing...

11
00:00:59,880 --> 00:01:00,960
Sweetie,

12
00:01:01,400 --> 00:01:02,560
you're burning up.

13
00:01:04,120 --> 00:01:05,200
Have you eaten yet?

14
00:01:07,080 --> 00:01:08,440
I'll go get your medicine.

15
00:01:08,720 --> 00:01:10,600
Eat something so you can take your meds, okay?

16
00:02:04,440 --> 00:02:05,240
P'Ing?

17
00:02:07,320 --> 00:02:08,720
What the hell is going on?

18
00:02:10,160 --> 00:02:11,320
Don't tell me...

19
00:02:13,720 --> 00:02:14,680
you've been holding me

20
00:02:14,720 --> 00:02:16,600
since we were rushed here.

21
00:02:18,920 --> 00:02:19,880
I haven't.

22
00:02:21,320 --> 00:02:24,680
Then why are you clinging to me like this?

23
00:02:24,760 --> 00:02:26,920
Is there a shortage of hospital beds?

24
00:02:27,520 --> 00:02:28,800
That's not it, either.

25
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:30,120
I see.

26
00:02:30,880 --> 00:02:34,280
You must have just been waiting...

27
00:02:34,320 --> 00:02:36,240
for the chance to cuddle up with me in bed.

28
00:02:39,079 --> 00:02:40,040
P'Ing,

29
00:02:42,560 --> 00:02:44,120
about what I said yesterday...

30
00:02:44,600 --> 00:02:45,720
You mean about last night?

31
00:02:48,720 --> 00:02:50,600
What about it? I don't seem to remember.

32
00:02:54,680 --> 00:02:55,960
Are you going back on your word?

33
00:02:56,440 --> 00:02:57,600
What do you mean?

34
00:02:58,480 --> 00:02:59,520
I do remember.

35
00:03:01,160 --> 00:03:02,560
It's good that you're okay.

36
00:03:12,680 --> 00:03:13,960
Same goes for you.

37
00:03:17,320 --> 00:03:18,160
Fine.

38
00:03:19,560 --> 00:03:21,880
I'll marry into your family.

39
00:03:23,520 --> 00:03:24,360
As for you,

40
00:03:25,600 --> 00:03:27,280
you have to be my bottom, though.

41
00:03:30,040 --> 00:03:31,200
You wish.

42
00:03:36,680 --> 00:03:39,360
This is actually nice.

43
00:03:46,350 --> 00:03:47,910
[Mom]

44
00:03:51,680 --> 00:03:52,440
Hello, Mom.

45
00:03:52,480 --> 00:03:53,840
Why didn't you pick up my calls?

46
00:03:54,040 --> 00:03:55,840
I was calling you all night.

47
00:03:55,880 --> 00:03:58,040
I'm at the Samui project with P'Ing.

48
00:03:58,880 --> 00:04:00,440
My phone happened to break,

49
00:04:00,720 --> 00:04:02,480
and it was pouring last night,

50
00:04:03,040 --> 00:04:04,560
so I just got it repaired.

51
00:04:04,560 --> 00:04:07,040
You mean Koh Samui?

52
00:04:07,880 --> 00:04:08,600
The news said

53
00:04:08,600 --> 00:04:10,840
the storm hit earlier than forecasted.

54
00:04:11,720 --> 00:04:13,280
You're okay, right?

55
00:04:14,240 --> 00:04:15,360
I'm fine.

56
00:04:15,920 --> 00:04:17,519
But the site inspection

57
00:04:17,519 --> 00:04:19,839
might be delayed by a few days.

58
00:04:20,800 --> 00:04:21,839
I'll be here for a while.

59
00:04:22,120 --> 00:04:25,400
Can you make it home this Saturday?

60
00:04:26,320 --> 00:04:29,720
I don't think I can, Mom.

61
00:04:30,240 --> 00:04:31,720
You and Dad don't have to worry.

62
00:04:32,480 --> 00:04:33,960
I can take care of myself.

63
00:04:34,720 --> 00:04:37,440
Okay, dear. See you.

64
00:04:37,960 --> 00:04:38,680
See you, Mom.

65
00:04:51,120 --> 00:04:52,680
We're in a hospital, you know.

66
00:04:59,920 --> 00:05:02,840
I've never done it in a hospital before.

67
00:05:19,800 --> 00:05:21,600
Let me lock the door first.

68
00:05:23,160 --> 00:05:24,880
You've learned something, haven't you?

69
00:05:37,920 --> 00:05:38,840
P'Ing...

70
00:05:40,680 --> 00:05:41,760
Are you alright?

71
00:05:42,760 --> 00:05:43,960
I'm not that badly hurt.

72
00:05:44,280 --> 00:05:45,920
I'll be fine after resting for a few days.

73
00:05:46,159 --> 00:05:48,320
Someone told Dad about what happened last night,

74
00:05:48,880 --> 00:05:50,680
so he told me to bring you home.

75
00:05:50,880 --> 00:05:52,040
It's nothing serious.

76
00:05:52,320 --> 00:05:54,440
Then I'll stay here with you.

77
00:05:54,480 --> 00:05:55,240
No need.

78
00:05:55,640 --> 00:05:57,159
I don't need anyone watching over me.

79
00:05:57,840 --> 00:05:58,440
Look.

80
00:06:03,200 --> 00:06:04,720
I can manage on my own.

81
00:06:05,600 --> 00:06:07,240
Aren't you supposed to be studying for your exams?

82
00:06:07,440 --> 00:06:08,320
How can my exams

83
00:06:08,560 --> 00:06:10,720
matter more than your safety?

84
00:06:17,320 --> 00:06:19,920
Yok will also be here, after all.

85
00:06:26,600 --> 00:06:28,440
Why are you just standing there? Sit down.

86
00:06:32,640 --> 00:06:33,640
Does it hurt?

87
00:06:34,320 --> 00:06:36,320
No, it's just a few scratches.

88
00:06:36,760 --> 00:06:38,080
I just need some rest.

89
00:06:45,080 --> 00:06:45,800
Yok,

90
00:06:46,920 --> 00:06:48,680
I want to talk to my brother in private.

91
00:06:50,760 --> 00:06:51,920
Excuse me.

92
00:06:53,480 --> 00:06:54,720
There you are.

93
00:06:55,040 --> 00:06:57,080
I was looking for you.

94
00:06:57,120 --> 00:06:57,840
Go back to your room

95
00:06:57,880 --> 00:07:00,160
and finish your IV drip, sir.

96
00:07:07,480 --> 00:07:08,240
Go on.

97
00:07:17,000 --> 00:07:18,160
Does it hurt a lot?

98
00:09:29,960 --> 00:09:30,600
Itt.

99
00:09:32,640 --> 00:09:33,200
Yok.

100
00:09:34,640 --> 00:09:36,320
You wanted to resign

101
00:09:36,560 --> 00:09:38,000
because of my brother, right?

102
00:09:43,680 --> 00:09:45,040
You're in love with him, aren't you?

103
00:09:49,400 --> 00:09:50,480
I'm sorry.

104
00:09:52,720 --> 00:09:53,480
Yok,

105
00:09:54,080 --> 00:09:55,400
you told me to fight

106
00:09:55,400 --> 00:09:56,680
and take my revenge.

107
00:09:56,960 --> 00:09:58,440
You got me to where I am now,

108
00:09:58,600 --> 00:10:00,840
but what you've done makes me feel like

109
00:10:00,880 --> 00:10:03,040
I've been betrayed by my best friend.

110
00:10:08,880 --> 00:10:10,800
I know I'm to blame for what happened,

111
00:10:10,800 --> 00:10:11,440
but...

112
00:10:12,720 --> 00:10:14,920
I don't think P'Ing is that bad.

113
00:10:15,360 --> 00:10:16,520
If you can,

114
00:10:17,400 --> 00:10:19,200
-you should talk to him... -About what?

115
00:10:19,800 --> 00:10:20,600
How?

116
00:10:21,480 --> 00:10:23,080
Are you not going to America anymore?

117
00:10:23,360 --> 00:10:24,840
I haven't signed the contract yet.

118
00:10:25,280 --> 00:10:26,200
There's still time.

119
00:10:29,160 --> 00:10:31,280
Maybe I'm jealous of you, Yok.

120
00:10:33,040 --> 00:10:34,200
P'Ing braved the storm to save you

121
00:10:34,200 --> 00:10:35,680
without caring about his own life.

122
00:10:36,600 --> 00:10:37,600
But you know

123
00:10:37,600 --> 00:10:38,720
what he's done to me.

124
00:10:40,560 --> 00:10:42,840
If he finds out I was plotting against him,

125
00:10:43,600 --> 00:10:45,160
do you think he'll spare me?

126
00:10:51,840 --> 00:10:53,040
Itt, hey...

127
00:10:53,800 --> 00:10:54,520
Itt.

128
00:10:55,040 --> 00:10:57,280
That money doesn't mean anything to him,

129
00:10:58,320 --> 00:11:00,880
but it's the only way out for me and my mom.

130
00:11:02,520 --> 00:11:04,200
And you gave me your word.

131
00:11:04,640 --> 00:11:05,720
In all these years,

132
00:11:05,720 --> 00:11:07,640
I've only ever asked you for one thing.

133
00:11:08,560 --> 00:11:09,840
Just one thing.

134
00:11:21,600 --> 00:11:22,320
Itt,

135
00:11:24,160 --> 00:11:25,000
I think...

136
00:11:28,040 --> 00:11:29,720
I'd better quit.

137
00:11:38,400 --> 00:11:40,080
I don't want to hurt him anymore.

138
00:11:43,960 --> 00:11:45,560
About the project in Pattaya,

139
00:11:46,360 --> 00:11:47,520
I'll transfer everything to you.

140
00:11:48,520 --> 00:11:49,800
I won't stand in your way,

141
00:11:49,880 --> 00:11:51,600
and I'll keep it a secret.

142
00:11:52,840 --> 00:11:54,680
But you have to promise me...

143
00:11:55,320 --> 00:11:56,800
that once you get the money,

144
00:11:58,080 --> 00:11:58,960
you'll stop.

145
00:12:09,600 --> 00:12:11,520
I knew you wouldn't change your mind.

146
00:12:13,440 --> 00:12:15,040
You don't have to resign from the company.

147
00:12:16,960 --> 00:12:18,800
I'll use my own company from now on.

148
00:12:19,400 --> 00:12:20,720
Think of it as a keepsake.

149
00:12:24,480 --> 00:12:26,440
I won't get you into any more trouble.

150
00:12:31,960 --> 00:12:32,640
Itt...

151
00:12:37,400 --> 00:12:39,360
Are we still friends?

152
00:12:43,000 --> 00:12:44,000
Of course.

153
00:12:45,240 --> 00:12:46,560
We'll always be friends.

154
00:12:49,040 --> 00:12:51,040
What are you going to do about P'Ing?

155
00:12:53,760 --> 00:12:55,200
I know him better than anyone.

156
00:12:56,760 --> 00:12:57,880
My brother...

157
00:12:58,240 --> 00:12:59,920
hates nothing more than being lied to.

158
00:13:01,360 --> 00:13:03,520
The second you helped me,

159
00:13:03,560 --> 00:13:04,920
you'd already betrayed him.

160
00:13:39,400 --> 00:13:40,560
Excuse me.

161
00:13:41,160 --> 00:13:42,520
The patient has just fallen asleep.

162
00:13:42,520 --> 00:13:44,960
Please don't disturb his rest right now.

163
00:13:45,880 --> 00:13:46,680
Okay.

164
00:14:16,800 --> 00:14:17,840
What's up, Young Master?

165
00:14:18,520 --> 00:14:19,280
Where are you?

166
00:14:19,320 --> 00:14:20,120
Are you bored?

167
00:14:20,480 --> 00:14:22,840
Or did you miss me?

168
00:14:23,280 --> 00:14:24,280
Are you free tonight?

169
00:14:26,240 --> 00:14:27,600
Are you asking me out?

170
00:14:28,000 --> 00:14:29,600
That's too bad, though.

171
00:14:29,960 --> 00:14:32,360
I already have a client to take care of.

172
00:14:32,840 --> 00:14:33,880
Name your price.

173
00:14:34,280 --> 00:14:35,800
From now on, you're on my dime,

174
00:14:36,360 --> 00:14:37,720
but the condition is...

175
00:14:38,120 --> 00:14:39,760
you can't see any other clients.

176
00:14:40,480 --> 00:14:40,960
And...

177
00:15:12,640 --> 00:15:13,480
You little Young Master.

178
00:15:17,840 --> 00:15:20,360
Remember to pay me when you wake up.

179
00:15:22,280 --> 00:15:23,720
You've got a good-looking face.

180
00:15:25,600 --> 00:15:26,640
You're loaded, too.

181
00:15:31,480 --> 00:15:33,520
What the hell is bothering you so much?

182
00:15:56,600 --> 00:15:57,800
Maybe you actually...

183
00:15:58,440 --> 00:15:59,920
missed me.

184
00:16:33,680 --> 00:16:34,640
Where am I?

185
00:16:45,840 --> 00:16:47,560
Eat it while it's still hot.

186
00:16:55,240 --> 00:16:58,320
Last night, you bought me off another client

187
00:16:58,680 --> 00:16:59,360
and got trashed.

188
00:16:59,360 --> 00:17:00,400
I had to carry you back.

189
00:17:00,600 --> 00:17:02,720
P.S. You still owe me

190
00:17:02,720 --> 00:17:04,560
for the money I lost out on last night.

191
00:17:04,560 --> 00:17:05,520
I'll let you run a tab for now.

192
00:17:10,760 --> 00:17:12,530
[From now on, I'm your only client.]

193
00:17:12,560 --> 00:17:13,990
[If you can't do that, return it to me.]

194
00:17:21,510 --> 00:17:23,700
[Whenever you miss me, that's when I get off work.]

195
00:17:23,730 --> 00:17:25,290
[I'm coming, then.]

196
00:17:25,319 --> 00:17:27,540
[My little caterpillar's in a hurry, huh?]

197
00:17:27,569 --> 00:17:28,930
[Caterpillar?]

198
00:17:28,950 --> 00:17:31,440
[I'm not going anywhere.]

199
00:17:54,040 --> 00:17:56,200
What the fuck?

200
00:17:57,160 --> 00:17:59,360
Is this my welcome back?

201
00:17:59,920 --> 00:18:01,880
Welcome back, sir.

202
00:18:01,920 --> 00:18:03,800
This is how much we've missed you

203
00:18:03,840 --> 00:18:06,160
while you were away.

204
00:18:09,000 --> 00:18:10,360
It's been tough for you, Secretary Piang.

205
00:18:11,560 --> 00:18:12,960
I'll give you five...

206
00:18:16,200 --> 00:18:17,280
Five?

207
00:18:18,240 --> 00:18:19,320
I'll give you triple your OT rate.

208
00:18:21,640 --> 00:18:24,040
But weren't you supposed to be sick?

209
00:18:24,040 --> 00:18:25,560
It looks like...

210
00:18:25,560 --> 00:18:28,560
you're much brighter than before.

211
00:18:28,640 --> 00:18:31,200
Oh, of course.

212
00:18:31,680 --> 00:18:33,920
When something good happens to you,

213
00:18:34,760 --> 00:18:36,440
it's natural to look radiant.

214
00:18:37,800 --> 00:18:41,080
Looks like having a life partner...

215
00:18:41,120 --> 00:18:42,720
I mean, a good business partner...

216
00:18:42,720 --> 00:18:46,720
makes work a lot more pleasant and productive.

217
00:18:47,600 --> 00:18:48,800
Since you said that,

218
00:18:49,320 --> 00:18:50,880
I'll cut it from triple to double.

219
00:18:52,840 --> 00:18:54,240
You do look brighter,

220
00:18:54,240 --> 00:18:55,920
-after all. -Here, Secretary Piang.

221
00:18:56,040 --> 00:18:57,280
Please schedule a meeting right away.

222
00:18:57,320 --> 00:18:59,680
The local leaders in Pattaya

223
00:18:59,720 --> 00:19:00,520
have already agreed.

224
00:19:00,560 --> 00:19:01,680
We only need one set of documents

225
00:19:01,720 --> 00:19:03,760
from Green Agriculture

226
00:19:03,800 --> 00:19:06,600
to start the project approval process.

227
00:19:06,640 --> 00:19:08,440
We'll discuss the details in the meeting.

228
00:19:08,480 --> 00:19:10,080
Understood. I'll get right on it.

229
00:19:11,440 --> 00:19:12,680
Make sure to submit that...

230
00:19:13,440 --> 00:19:13,840
Yes?

231
00:19:13,880 --> 00:19:15,960
You're getting five times the OT.

232
00:19:16,440 --> 00:19:19,320
Whoa, okay. Thank you, sir.

233
00:20:00,720 --> 00:20:02,080
Thank you.

234
00:20:07,240 --> 00:20:08,640
P'Ing,

235
00:20:08,760 --> 00:20:09,920
I missed you.

236
00:20:09,960 --> 00:20:10,760
What?

237
00:20:11,080 --> 00:20:12,880
Weren't you just here to deliver dinner?

238
00:20:21,560 --> 00:20:22,480
Hold on.

239
00:20:22,840 --> 00:20:23,920
Close the door first.

240
00:20:24,120 --> 00:20:24,920
Hey.

241
00:20:38,560 --> 00:20:39,320
Hey,

242
00:20:39,840 --> 00:20:41,520
it'll turn into mush if you keep doing that.

243
00:20:44,120 --> 00:20:44,960
I'm sorry.

244
00:20:48,080 --> 00:20:49,080
What are you sorry for?

245
00:20:50,560 --> 00:20:51,440
Alright.

246
00:20:53,520 --> 00:20:54,480
Just say it.

247
00:21:02,280 --> 00:21:05,360
It's about that tryout at the boxing gym.

248
00:21:06,800 --> 00:21:07,920
I passed.

249
00:21:08,560 --> 00:21:10,240
They want to sign me to a contract

250
00:21:11,920 --> 00:21:13,760
and have me train in America.

251
00:21:23,520 --> 00:21:24,520
Are you serious?

252
00:21:25,040 --> 00:21:25,800
Wow.

253
00:21:26,400 --> 00:21:28,120
You're amazing, you know that?

254
00:21:28,480 --> 00:21:29,440
It's America.

255
00:21:29,480 --> 00:21:30,840
You must be incredible.

256
00:21:31,040 --> 00:21:31,920
Let me give you a reward.

257
00:21:36,040 --> 00:21:36,960
What's wrong?

258
00:21:38,520 --> 00:21:40,160
What's with that face?

259
00:21:40,760 --> 00:21:41,520
Hey.

260
00:21:41,920 --> 00:21:44,080
You thought I wouldn't let you go, right?

261
00:21:46,640 --> 00:21:47,680
Fine, I'll admit

262
00:21:47,680 --> 00:21:50,920
that I wanted to keep you chained to my side.

263
00:21:51,960 --> 00:21:53,080
But not anymore.

264
00:21:53,480 --> 00:21:54,440
You know why?

265
00:21:55,400 --> 00:21:58,440
Because your heart belongs to me now.

266
00:21:58,440 --> 00:22:00,880
No matter where in the world you go,

267
00:22:01,040 --> 00:22:02,760
you'll still be thinking of me.

268
00:22:08,360 --> 00:22:09,000
Oh...

269
00:22:10,840 --> 00:22:12,440
I don't want to go anymore.

270
00:22:13,040 --> 00:22:13,920
Why not?

271
00:22:14,840 --> 00:22:15,640
Hey.

272
00:22:16,040 --> 00:22:16,600
Look.

273
00:22:18,440 --> 00:22:19,720
You trained your heart out for this.

274
00:22:19,760 --> 00:22:21,040
Why are you backing out now?

275
00:22:22,560 --> 00:22:23,920
I see.

276
00:22:24,600 --> 00:22:26,320
Because I'm too hot, right?

277
00:22:26,720 --> 00:22:28,920
No wonder you can't keep your mouth off my neck.

278
00:22:29,320 --> 00:22:29,880
Is that it?

279
00:22:30,720 --> 00:22:31,520
Why?

280
00:22:31,720 --> 00:22:33,440
Why give up after so much hard work?

281
00:22:34,680 --> 00:22:36,320
Hey, be honest with me.

282
00:22:38,400 --> 00:22:40,280
Do you feel a rush when you're in the ring?

283
00:22:41,560 --> 00:22:42,240
I do.

284
00:22:42,280 --> 00:22:43,040
There you go.

285
00:22:43,920 --> 00:22:45,680
If you feel that rush, give it everything you've got.

286
00:22:45,720 --> 00:22:47,440
Do you have any idea how rare it is...

287
00:22:48,640 --> 00:22:50,480
to find something that gives you that rush?

288
00:22:50,880 --> 00:22:52,040
It's hard to come by.

289
00:22:52,280 --> 00:22:53,200
You think I can't afford

290
00:22:53,240 --> 00:22:54,680
a ticket to America

291
00:22:54,680 --> 00:22:56,200
to visit you?

292
00:22:58,520 --> 00:23:00,320
I could book a flight right now if I wanted to.

293
00:23:02,400 --> 00:23:03,320
But...

294
00:23:04,280 --> 00:23:06,520
I'm not sure if my dad will let me go.

295
00:23:08,120 --> 00:23:08,760
He wants me

296
00:23:08,760 --> 00:23:10,440
to help my brother with the family business.

297
00:23:10,440 --> 00:23:11,200
And?

298
00:23:11,880 --> 00:23:13,640
Is that business really that important?

299
00:23:13,680 --> 00:23:15,520
Is it more important than your dream?

300
00:23:15,800 --> 00:23:17,280
Just do both.

301
00:23:17,360 --> 00:23:18,120
Simple as that.

302
00:23:18,560 --> 00:23:20,160
Do what you have to do, then tell him later.

303
00:23:20,280 --> 00:23:21,480
As for keeping it a secret,

304
00:23:22,440 --> 00:23:23,840
you can count on me.

305
00:23:28,680 --> 00:23:29,760
Well...

306
00:23:31,240 --> 00:23:32,400
Will you wait for me?

307
00:23:32,960 --> 00:23:34,560
You really think I will?

308
00:23:36,080 --> 00:23:37,160
I'd definitely...

309
00:23:37,920 --> 00:23:40,040
be booking the first flight out to see you

310
00:23:40,080 --> 00:23:42,120
in America.

311
00:23:42,280 --> 00:23:43,160
Listen to me.

312
00:23:43,160 --> 00:23:44,680
If I fly all that way to America

313
00:23:44,680 --> 00:23:46,240
and you haven't won a single title,

314
00:23:46,280 --> 00:23:48,240
I'm going to jump-kick you right in the face.

315
00:23:48,280 --> 00:23:50,520
It's a long flight. Got it?

316
00:23:55,280 --> 00:23:56,120
P'Ing...

317
00:23:57,000 --> 00:23:57,920
What if...

318
00:23:58,680 --> 00:24:00,720
I'm not the person you think I am?

319
00:24:01,040 --> 00:24:01,640
What would you do?

320
00:24:01,680 --> 00:24:03,160
Jeez, what's with you today?

321
00:24:03,200 --> 00:24:04,440
Why so dramatic?

322
00:24:04,920 --> 00:24:06,840
Are you scamming me out of my money?

323
00:24:07,120 --> 00:24:09,040
Or are you trying to steal my heart?

324
00:24:10,440 --> 00:24:12,280
I don't know if you realize, but...

325
00:24:12,320 --> 00:24:14,360
I've already stolen yours.

326
00:24:18,280 --> 00:24:19,360
Listen to me.

327
00:24:21,280 --> 00:24:22,320
You know,

328
00:24:24,160 --> 00:24:25,320
when I choose someone,

329
00:24:27,720 --> 00:24:28,840
they're bound to be the best.

330
00:24:33,720 --> 00:24:34,560
Right.

331
00:24:38,440 --> 00:24:40,120
Oh, still worried?

332
00:24:50,680 --> 00:24:51,520
Come here.

333
00:24:52,320 --> 00:24:53,680
Come on.

334
00:24:54,280 --> 00:24:55,360
Get over here.

335
00:24:55,400 --> 00:24:57,200
Look at you, acting like a clingy bottom.

336
00:24:57,240 --> 00:24:59,080
What was all that tough talk for?

337
00:24:59,120 --> 00:25:00,920
Come on, just turn around already.

338
00:25:00,920 --> 00:25:01,880
I'm telling you.

339
00:25:01,920 --> 00:25:03,600
Just turn around, and that's it.

340
00:25:03,640 --> 00:25:05,720
Then everything will be just fine.

341
00:25:05,760 --> 00:25:06,200
No.

342
00:25:06,240 --> 00:25:08,240
Where is all this strength coming from?

343
00:25:09,480 --> 00:25:11,200
We just did it. You want another round already?

344
00:25:11,320 --> 00:25:13,200
Turn around. I won't this time.

345
00:25:13,520 --> 00:25:14,320
I said I'm not turning.

346
00:25:14,360 --> 00:25:15,560
You need to turn around, you...

347
00:25:33,560 --> 00:25:34,560
Let's go inside.

348
00:25:44,680 --> 00:25:46,280
When do you leave for training in America?

349
00:25:47,080 --> 00:25:48,280
September 15th.

350
00:25:54,720 --> 00:25:56,080
Consider yourself officially taken.

351
00:25:56,840 --> 00:25:57,800
From now on,

352
00:25:58,160 --> 00:26:00,280
you're eating out of my hand.

353
00:26:01,080 --> 00:26:02,480
I'm not letting you go anywhere.

354
00:26:04,720 --> 00:26:05,440
Okay.

355
00:26:20,280 --> 00:26:21,200
I used to think

356
00:26:21,200 --> 00:26:23,720
that living alone was the ultimate freedom,

357
00:26:24,080 --> 00:26:26,160
but seeing you moving in like this...

358
00:26:26,200 --> 00:26:28,440
I don't know why, but it makes me feel so happy.

359
00:26:28,480 --> 00:26:30,560
Can't you stay for more than just the weekends?

360
00:26:30,840 --> 00:26:33,000
Why not stay every day?

361
00:26:33,680 --> 00:26:35,280
Give you an inch, and you take a mile, huh?

362
00:26:49,210 --> 00:26:50,520
[There's food in the fridge. Microwave it first.]

363
00:26:50,560 --> 00:26:52,000
Where should I put my things?

364
00:26:52,200 --> 00:26:53,120
Right here.

365
00:26:53,440 --> 00:26:54,360
This is your spot.

366
00:26:57,720 --> 00:26:58,920
You have those, too?

367
00:26:58,920 --> 00:26:59,960
For dusting, you know.

368
00:27:00,000 --> 00:27:01,160
Is this all you have?

369
00:27:01,440 --> 00:27:02,880
I don't have as much stuff as you.

370
00:27:03,080 --> 00:27:03,880
Hey.

371
00:27:04,400 --> 00:27:05,520
Kiddo.

372
00:27:06,360 --> 00:27:08,040
Let me tell you something.

373
00:27:08,320 --> 00:27:10,440
My things aren't just my stuff, you know.

374
00:27:11,320 --> 00:27:12,440
They're my taste.

375
00:27:17,060 --> 00:27:19,220
[No classes tomorrow. Wanna hit the supermarket?]

376
00:27:21,490 --> 00:27:23,020
[Tonight, you're going to be my bottom.]

377
00:27:23,040 --> 00:27:24,160
[In your dreams.]

378
00:27:27,360 --> 00:27:28,280
P'Ing,

379
00:27:28,400 --> 00:27:30,280
stay still. Where's the key?

380
00:27:30,320 --> 00:27:31,320
In the pocket.

381
00:27:31,600 --> 00:27:33,160
-Pocket? -Yeah.

382
00:27:34,040 --> 00:27:35,320
Lower.

383
00:27:35,680 --> 00:27:36,920
Lower.

384
00:27:37,320 --> 00:27:38,760
Oh, you got it.

385
00:27:40,200 --> 00:27:41,520
Here it is.

386
00:27:44,920 --> 00:27:46,320
Stay still, P'Ing.

387
00:27:47,040 --> 00:27:48,200
Yok,

388
00:27:48,200 --> 00:27:49,200
give me a kiss.

389
00:27:54,960 --> 00:27:56,280
Yok.

390
00:27:57,120 --> 00:27:58,320
Do you want to sleep outside tonight?

391
00:28:12,720 --> 00:28:14,000
Now that's more like it.

392
00:28:14,040 --> 00:28:14,960
P'Ing...

393
00:28:15,840 --> 00:28:17,600
There's still more space.

394
00:28:18,200 --> 00:28:19,280
Come here.

395
00:28:21,280 --> 00:28:22,920
You're getting stretched tonight.

396
00:28:30,080 --> 00:28:31,720
A new healthy dish for you.

397
00:28:31,720 --> 00:28:33,040
Give it a taste.

398
00:28:41,120 --> 00:28:42,640
It's spicy chicken wing soup,

399
00:28:42,640 --> 00:28:44,800
but it's stuffed with chilies.

400
00:28:46,080 --> 00:28:47,000
Is it good?

401
00:28:48,920 --> 00:28:50,280
Wanna know how good it is?

402
00:28:50,320 --> 00:28:50,960
Get over here.

403
00:28:51,000 --> 00:28:52,200
Feel the spice.

404
00:28:52,240 --> 00:28:53,400
Come here.

405
00:28:55,600 --> 00:28:56,400
Is it spicy?

406
00:28:56,440 --> 00:28:57,080
Is it hot?

407
00:28:57,650 --> 00:28:58,670
[Secret Recipe for Shrimp Porridge]

408
00:28:58,700 --> 00:29:00,220
[Main ingredients: Shrimp, rice]

409
00:29:33,280 --> 00:29:34,680
This food here is pretty good.

410
00:29:35,000 --> 00:29:35,800
Yeah.

411
00:29:37,160 --> 00:29:38,120
So in love, huh?

412
00:29:41,120 --> 00:29:42,000
Mm.

413
00:29:44,680 --> 00:29:46,280
Pineapple. My favorite.

414
00:29:52,280 --> 00:29:53,360
Why aren't you picking up?

415
00:29:54,720 --> 00:29:55,480
Oh.

416
00:29:56,920 --> 00:29:58,520
It's just a telemarketer.

417
00:29:59,480 --> 00:30:00,320
It's nothing.

418
00:30:03,000 --> 00:30:05,160
Does the telemarketer's name happen to be Jelly?

419
00:30:05,200 --> 00:30:06,280
Jelly Bear.

420
00:30:09,440 --> 00:30:10,640
Okay, you win.

421
00:30:10,840 --> 00:30:12,080
Since we started seeing each other again,

422
00:30:12,080 --> 00:30:13,440
I haven't contacted him once.

423
00:30:13,440 --> 00:30:15,320
I haven't even said anything, P'Ing.

424
00:30:25,440 --> 00:30:27,680
I'll have Vince take care of it,

425
00:30:27,680 --> 00:30:29,840
and he'll never contact me again.

426
00:30:32,640 --> 00:30:33,440
Are you jealous?

427
00:30:34,960 --> 00:30:37,640
Is this what you look like when you're jealous?

428
00:30:39,120 --> 00:30:39,920
Jealous, aren't you?

429
00:30:40,320 --> 00:30:41,080
You jealous?

430
00:30:41,320 --> 00:30:42,720
-P'Ing. -What?

431
00:30:42,840 --> 00:30:43,920
There are people around.

432
00:30:43,920 --> 00:30:44,800
Just eat.

433
00:30:48,200 --> 00:30:49,320
Eat a lot, okay?

434
00:30:50,440 --> 00:30:51,400
So you'll have some energy.

435
00:30:52,640 --> 00:30:53,640
For what?

436
00:30:53,680 --> 00:30:56,280
Just in case you get hungry again after we leave.

437
00:31:00,000 --> 00:31:01,240
Aren't you going to eat?

438
00:31:02,240 --> 00:31:03,040
I am.

439
00:31:03,840 --> 00:31:04,920
The food?

440
00:31:05,440 --> 00:31:06,400
No, you.

441
00:31:06,760 --> 00:31:07,640
Tonight.

442
00:31:07,800 --> 00:31:09,920
The interior construction

443
00:31:09,960 --> 00:31:11,760
is now 85 percent complete.

444
00:31:11,840 --> 00:31:13,080
We need to finalize

445
00:31:13,080 --> 00:31:14,520
the interior design style

446
00:31:14,560 --> 00:31:16,760
and the core concept of the project first.

447
00:31:18,120 --> 00:31:19,920
Regarding the style and the ideas,

448
00:31:21,840 --> 00:31:22,880
why don't you prove yourself?

449
00:31:22,920 --> 00:31:24,800
Tell me what you think.

450
00:31:30,160 --> 00:31:32,000
I think a smart theme

451
00:31:32,040 --> 00:31:34,680
or something futuristic would be quite interesting.

452
00:31:34,680 --> 00:31:37,400
A smart or futuristic concept?

453
00:31:37,440 --> 00:31:39,560
Those concepts have been used for plenty of projects.

454
00:31:39,720 --> 00:31:41,080
This project we're working on

455
00:31:41,120 --> 00:31:42,880
is not just any ordinary project.

456
00:31:43,120 --> 00:31:46,320
It needs to have soul, be captivating,

457
00:31:47,360 --> 00:31:48,560
and feel warm.

458
00:31:50,120 --> 00:31:52,280
For example, the word...

459
00:31:53,280 --> 00:31:54,080
-Home. -Home.

460
00:32:07,320 --> 00:32:08,160
Mr. Ing,

461
00:32:08,560 --> 00:32:09,680
something urgent came up.

462
00:32:10,400 --> 00:32:11,520
Come in.

463
00:32:15,920 --> 00:32:16,720
What is it?

464
00:32:17,200 --> 00:32:19,960
Green Agriculture just informed us

465
00:32:20,080 --> 00:32:21,520
they are terminating the partnership.

466
00:32:22,600 --> 00:32:23,560
What's their reason?

467
00:32:24,560 --> 00:32:25,440
They only stated

468
00:32:25,440 --> 00:32:27,080
that it's due to a change in corporate strategy,

469
00:32:27,120 --> 00:32:29,160
and they no longer wish to pursue this business direction.

470
00:32:29,280 --> 00:32:30,400
Dammit.

471
00:32:30,880 --> 00:32:32,560
Do they think I'm some kind of joke?

472
00:32:33,960 --> 00:32:35,600
Jeez, they hung up on me.

473
00:32:42,440 --> 00:32:43,800
Hello, Director Pha-nu.

474
00:32:43,800 --> 00:32:46,480
I'm calling about Green Agriculture.

475
00:32:46,520 --> 00:32:48,280
Do you know if there's any problem?

476
00:32:51,480 --> 00:32:52,160
I see.

477
00:32:53,360 --> 00:32:54,360
Understood.

478
00:32:54,960 --> 00:32:56,920
Please let me know if there are any updates.

479
00:32:58,200 --> 00:32:59,320
Dammit.

480
00:33:00,280 --> 00:33:02,400
Does the couple have any idea

481
00:33:02,440 --> 00:33:04,720
how much we spent to acquire this land?

482
00:33:05,640 --> 00:33:07,840
What should we do next, P'Ing?

483
00:33:08,320 --> 00:33:10,520
Get them in here to talk to me.

484
00:33:11,560 --> 00:33:12,440
-Will do. -Jeez.

485
00:33:15,400 --> 00:33:16,200
Come in.

486
00:33:22,440 --> 00:33:23,560
What happened?

487
00:33:28,040 --> 00:33:30,040
Green Agriculture pulled out of the project.

488
00:33:37,400 --> 00:33:38,880
So suddenly?

489
00:33:39,440 --> 00:33:41,560
But there's some good news.

490
00:33:41,840 --> 00:33:43,760
Regarding the land in Phuket we discussed earlier,

491
00:33:43,800 --> 00:33:45,440
the survey team has already sent the documents.

492
00:33:45,520 --> 00:33:47,920
They say it's a large plot in an excellent location.

493
00:33:48,320 --> 00:33:49,440
The government is also showing interest

494
00:33:49,440 --> 00:33:50,880
since it's a very promising project.

495
00:33:52,400 --> 00:33:53,320
Here it is.

496
00:33:54,200 --> 00:33:55,120
Right.

497
00:33:55,920 --> 00:33:57,400
At least there's some good news.

498
00:33:57,960 --> 00:33:59,120
Contact this team immediately

499
00:33:59,160 --> 00:34:00,720
and have our team survey the site.

500
00:34:00,760 --> 00:34:01,520
Understood.

501
00:34:03,720 --> 00:34:04,560
Mr. Ing,

502
00:34:05,600 --> 00:34:06,920
I'd like to go with Itt as well.

503
00:34:06,920 --> 00:34:07,640
No need.

504
00:34:11,239 --> 00:34:12,880
I want you to look after...

505
00:34:15,320 --> 00:34:16,280
our home.

506
00:34:19,560 --> 00:34:20,360
What?

507
00:34:21,520 --> 00:34:22,800
Isn't it already settled

508
00:34:22,840 --> 00:34:24,600
that you'd be in charge of this project?

509
00:34:31,600 --> 00:34:32,360
Okay.

510
00:34:32,920 --> 00:34:34,719
I'll follow up on it as quickly as I can.

511
00:34:36,000 --> 00:34:36,639
Mm.

512
00:34:38,719 --> 00:34:40,280
Anything else?

513
00:34:40,679 --> 00:34:42,760
Oh, that's all.

514
00:34:42,800 --> 00:34:43,840
Then go.

515
00:34:59,000 --> 00:35:02,360
Ugh, it's just one thing after another.

516
00:35:07,640 --> 00:35:08,880
Do you see...

517
00:35:09,480 --> 00:35:13,280
just how difficult it is to do business?

518
00:35:13,440 --> 00:35:14,640
Before one job is even finished,

519
00:35:14,680 --> 00:35:16,680
another one runs into problems.

520
00:35:21,040 --> 00:35:24,600
hat's how hard it is to earn money

521
00:35:38,440 --> 00:35:40,000
As for the Pattaya project,

522
00:35:40,040 --> 00:35:41,200
don't tell your brother just yet.

523
00:35:41,920 --> 00:35:43,200
Wait until the director informs him first.

524
00:35:43,240 --> 00:35:44,280
Understood.

525
00:35:49,120 --> 00:35:50,040
P'Ing?

526
00:35:50,440 --> 00:35:51,440
Is that Pite?

527
00:35:52,880 --> 00:35:53,640
Hey, Pite.

528
00:35:53,640 --> 00:35:54,160
Watch out.

529
00:35:54,200 --> 00:35:56,560
Where do you think you're going? Come here, you idiot.

530
00:35:57,680 --> 00:35:58,720
Calm down.

531
00:35:58,760 --> 00:36:00,920
-That jerk. -Please calm down.

532
00:36:01,560 --> 00:36:02,880
You're running away from me?

533
00:36:03,200 --> 00:36:03,840
Fine.

534
00:36:05,000 --> 00:36:06,040
You'll see what's coming to you.

535
00:36:12,640 --> 00:36:13,400
Hello.

536
00:36:13,920 --> 00:36:16,160
Find out where Pite is staying.

537
00:36:17,000 --> 00:36:17,720
Yeah.

538
00:36:18,200 --> 00:36:19,560
And ask the military

539
00:36:19,560 --> 00:36:21,680
if they're still accepting volunteer recruits.

540
00:36:21,800 --> 00:36:23,000
I'm sending him into the army.

541
00:36:24,040 --> 00:36:24,800
Okay.

542
00:36:25,360 --> 00:36:26,640
Send him as far away as possible.

543
00:36:27,440 --> 00:36:28,240
Make it happen.

544
00:36:32,600 --> 00:36:34,160
You're sending him to the military?

545
00:36:35,080 --> 00:36:35,920
Just look at him.

546
00:36:36,120 --> 00:36:37,880
All he does is cause more trouble.

547
00:36:38,120 --> 00:36:39,600
I can't clean up after him anymore.

548
00:36:42,640 --> 00:36:44,680
I thought you'd have someone beat him up.

549
00:36:46,520 --> 00:36:48,000
He's still my cousin.

550
00:36:50,920 --> 00:36:52,160
If I don't straighten him out now,

551
00:36:52,200 --> 00:36:53,760
he'll be ruined for life.

552
00:36:55,880 --> 00:36:56,880
We're going to have a blast.

553
00:36:56,880 --> 00:36:59,280
Don't come crying back to me, you little jerk.

554
00:36:59,960 --> 00:37:00,920
Take it easy.

555
00:37:05,080 --> 00:37:05,800
Yok.

556
00:37:17,600 --> 00:37:18,720
What's this?

557
00:37:20,880 --> 00:37:22,320
Open it and see for yourself.

558
00:37:48,680 --> 00:37:49,480
What?

559
00:37:50,320 --> 00:37:52,360
You looked so shocked at first.

560
00:37:53,480 --> 00:37:54,880
Thought it was a ring, huh?

561
00:37:57,640 --> 00:37:59,960
I was just gonna give you the key,

562
00:38:00,000 --> 00:38:01,880
but that didn't feel grand enough,

563
00:38:01,880 --> 00:38:04,840
so I got you a box to go with it.

564
00:38:04,880 --> 00:38:06,160
It's more fitting for someone of my status.

565
00:38:08,600 --> 00:38:09,680
I know that right now,

566
00:38:09,720 --> 00:38:10,760
it might be impossible

567
00:38:10,800 --> 00:38:12,440
for you to move into my house,

568
00:38:12,840 --> 00:38:14,400
but you've got the key now.

569
00:38:15,120 --> 00:38:17,480
Just think of this place as your home.

570
00:38:18,960 --> 00:38:20,680
You're always welcome here.

571
00:38:23,880 --> 00:38:25,280
Thank you, P'Ing.

572
00:38:29,280 --> 00:38:32,320
I'll hire someone to scrub the pool clean

573
00:38:32,360 --> 00:38:33,560
and make the water

574
00:38:33,600 --> 00:38:35,520
crystal clear. How's that?

575
00:38:36,440 --> 00:38:38,520
Then we can have an underwater date.

576
00:38:39,800 --> 00:38:41,240
I have to go home today.

577
00:38:41,280 --> 00:38:42,840
Then go ahead.

578
00:38:43,840 --> 00:38:45,440
I wouldn't want you neglecting your duties.

579
00:38:47,640 --> 00:38:51,240
How about the day after tomorrow?

580
00:38:52,040 --> 00:38:52,800
Alright.

581
00:38:53,360 --> 00:38:56,600
I'll pick out some sexy swimwear,

582
00:38:57,320 --> 00:38:59,120
but I doubt I'll be wearing it for very long

583
00:38:59,160 --> 00:39:01,680
'cause you'll definitely be stripping me bare.

584
00:39:01,720 --> 00:39:03,400
If you say one more word,

585
00:39:04,880 --> 00:39:06,160
I'm not going home.

586
00:39:13,960 --> 00:39:15,120
I'm off.

587
00:39:20,960 --> 00:39:25,320
Should I go with leopard print or cherry blossoms?

588
00:39:29,560 --> 00:39:31,000
Wait, Yok.

589
00:39:33,960 --> 00:39:35,840
If I gave you a ring, would you take it?

590
00:39:38,480 --> 00:39:39,720
What did you just say?

591
00:39:45,720 --> 00:39:46,440
Nothing.

592
00:39:46,840 --> 00:39:48,360
Just telling you to get home safe.

593
00:39:50,000 --> 00:39:50,960
Bye.

594
00:40:10,120 --> 00:40:11,160
But there's some good news.

595
00:40:11,600 --> 00:40:13,440
Regarding the land in Phuket we discussed earlier,

596
00:40:13,480 --> 00:40:15,200
the survey team has already sent the documents.

597
00:40:15,240 --> 00:40:17,640
They say it's a large plot in an excellent location.

598
00:40:17,680 --> 00:40:18,800
The government is also showing interest

599
00:40:18,800 --> 00:40:20,240
since it's a very promising project.

600
00:40:31,200 --> 00:40:32,240
Hello, Yok?

601
00:40:32,600 --> 00:40:33,640
Hello, P'Phet.

602
00:40:34,200 --> 00:40:36,160
Could you put me in touch with Director Phadung

603
00:40:36,160 --> 00:40:38,760
from the Phuket Development Department?

604
00:40:38,920 --> 00:40:41,200
Director Phadung? Right now?

605
00:40:42,360 --> 00:40:43,360
I have some questions

606
00:40:43,360 --> 00:40:44,760
about the project.

607
00:40:45,720 --> 00:40:47,720
Sure, I'll send you his number.

608
00:40:47,880 --> 00:40:48,680
Thank you.

609
00:40:55,160 --> 00:40:57,960
Itt, I hope it's not you.

610
00:41:06,400 --> 00:41:07,920
I thought this project should've been

611
00:41:07,920 --> 00:41:10,240
a perfect wrap-up before you left for America.

612
00:41:10,280 --> 00:41:11,640
Dammit.

613
00:41:11,720 --> 00:41:12,840
We've been played for fools.

614
00:41:12,880 --> 00:41:13,880
You told me

615
00:41:13,880 --> 00:41:15,560
that there was no way you'd ever be into guys.

616
00:41:16,520 --> 00:41:18,040
I admit...

617
00:41:18,080 --> 00:41:19,400
that I act like a tyrant

618
00:41:19,440 --> 00:41:20,400
and have a nasty temper,

619
00:41:20,440 --> 00:41:22,000
but I've never tried to hurt anyone.

620
00:41:22,040 --> 00:41:24,200
You think you can just play me for a fool?

621
00:41:25,040 --> 00:41:26,280
You wanna die that badly?

622
00:41:27,640 --> 00:41:28,760
Okay, maybe a little bit.

623
00:41:30,360 --> 00:41:32,080
Every time I ask you something, you know nothing.

624
00:41:32,080 --> 00:41:33,200
Dammit.

625
00:41:33,960 --> 00:41:35,200
Pite, start talking.

626
00:41:35,240 --> 00:41:36,680
Hey, P'Ing.

627
00:41:38,320 --> 00:41:39,560
I need to have a word with you.

628
00:41:41,120 --> 00:41:42,320
Dammit.

629
00:41:45,240 --> 00:41:48,360
[The UNCUT version of Fool in Love]

630
00:41:48,390 --> 00:41:51,550
[is exclusively available on iQIYI and iQ.com]
